{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776193882,"nonce":"0QSGsfEJpeqFe+Qt2x8JP7HzUjU=","title":"OpenCode: tool_use parsing doesn't extract part.tool structure","message":"## Problem\n\nOpenCode's stream-json format wraps tool info in a `part` object:\n```json\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"part\":{\"tool\":\"bash\",\"state\":{\"input\":{\"command\":\"ls\"}}}}\n```\n\nCurrent parsing looks for `name` or `tool` at top level, missing `part.tool`. This causes tool calls to show as `?: {}` in logs.\n\n## Tests (write first, must fail before implementation)\n- tests/test_opencode_agent.py::test_parse_tool_use_part_wrapped\n  Assert: parsing `{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"part\":{\"tool\":\"bash\",\"state\":{\"input\":{\"cmd\":\"ls\"}}}}` extracts tool name \"bash\" and input\n\n## Files\n- adapters/agents/opencode.py (modify)\n- tests/test_opencode_agent.py (modify)\n\n## Implementation\n1. In `_parse()` for `tool_use` events, check `ev.get(\"part\", {})` first\n2. Extract tool name from `part.tool` or fall back to `ev.get(\"name\", ev.get(\"tool\", \"?\"))`\n3. Extract input from `part.state.input` or fall back to `ev.get(\"input\", ev.get(\"arguments\", {}))`\n\n## Patterns to follow\n```python\npart = ev.get(\"part\", {})\nname = part.get(\"tool\") or ev.get(\"name\", ev.get(\"tool\", \"?\"))\nstate = part.get(\"state\", {})\ninp = state.get(\"input\") or ev.get(\"input\", ev.get(\"arguments\", {}))\n```\n\nREQ: REQ-031","files":null}]}